meta {
  name: Stage KEM key (POST /v1/kem-key)
  type: http
  seq: 170
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/kem-key
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{sessionToken}}
}

vars:pre-request {
  baseUrl: http://localhost:8080
}

docs {
  # POST /v1/kem-key

  Stage a fresh Spaces KEM key for the account (ADR-0043). Space writes answer
  `KemKeyNotPublished` until the account's DID document publishes its active KEM key as
  `#atproto_kem`; this is how an account installs or rotates it. Always mints a new key,
  replacing any key staged earlier.

  - **did:plc / self-hosted did:web:** returns `status: "staged"`. Publish the key (a
    wallet-signed PLC op, or an updated `did.json`), then call `/v1/kem-key/complete`.
  - **Custos-hosted did:web:** Custos writes the key into the served document, promotes it,
    and emits `#identity` at once; returns `status: "published"`.

  Authenticate as the account owner (wallet session token or full-access OAuth/XRPC token;
  agent-derived and app-password credentials refused).

  ## Response (200)

  ```json
  { "kemKey": "did:key:zDn...", "status": "staged" }
  ```

  ## Errors

  - `401` / `403` — missing/invalid credential, or an agent-derived/app-password token
  - `503` — signing-key master key not configured
}
